Warhammer 40k Inquisitor Mota  places the secret agents of the grim  future into an action-rpg and pits them  against the various enemies of mankind  your mission is to purge the Imperium of  men from corruption and to achieve this  goal you must fight in this violent  universe battles are not only vicious  and bloody but they also feel as real as  possible just like the fully  destructible environments in the game  Kombat surf has officially spectacular  reminder that in this future there is  only war every bolt of shots every chain  sword strike has an impact hits slowed  down enemies grenade blasts who send  heretics flying opponents fall down and  try to get back on their feet  unholy armor shatters to pieces carnage  in shoes in addition to all that the  more challenging fights just got some  extra flavor aimed attacks at joint foes  can destroy body parts getting rid of  special abilities by shooting up a  weapon arm you can make sure that you're  at least safe from the deadly fire  take your time intact those monsters  apart piece by piece  the game evokes a sense of brutal  warfare where no one is safe you can use  that to your advantage when you're  fighting the filth of chaos from time to  time you'll face demons that simply  don't care about their king and gladly  sacrifice their own in the crossfire  violence begets violence and sometimes  you'll need to strike down as brutally  as possible fatality is an integral part  of the game where each pass can use  special execution moves to finish off  most creatures and they all perish  differently  Inquisitor Mota is not for the  faint-hearted inquisitors must wait into  the thick of the battle where gushing  blood spatters on the walls spilled  entrails stains the floor severed limbs  twitch among the Fallen bodies there are  countless ways to dispose of the enemies  of the mighty Imperium and in this game  you'll have your chance to try them or  incinerate your foes cut them to pieces  blast them to smithereens or use the  elements of the environment against them  in this universe you need to fight fire  with fire and for this reason blood and  gore plays an important part in  Inquisitor mater  welcome to the grim world of Warhammer  40k
 

